{"id": "EUVD-2026-45447", "enisaUuid": "e2358d6f-0091-3627-8e25-55e5d4257755", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdgpu: zero-initialize GART table on allocation\n\nGART TLB is flushed after unmapping but not after mapping. Since\namdgpu_bo_create_kernel() does not zero-initialize the buffer, when a\nsingle PTE is written the TLB may speculatively load other uninitialized\nentries from the same cacheline. Those garbage entries can appear valid,\nand a subsequent write to another PTE in the same cacheline may cause the\nGPU to use a stale garbage PTE from the TLB.\n\nFix this by calling memset_io() to zero-initialize the GART table with\ngart_pte_flags immediately after allocation.\n\nUsing AMDGPU_GEM_CREATE_VRAM_CLEARED, SDMA-based clear will not work\nsince SDMA needs GART to be initialized to work.\n\n(cherry picked from commit d9af8263b82b6eaa60c5718e0c6631c5037e4b24)", "datePublished": "2026-07-19T10:01:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:07:45", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/40df11255d71b02e20e70579f1b12b687e396e26", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/91fbb5e635c8fb1b49e15c19da06480089ef719f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ae8b9e74bab94aab1d79f1688129bcc61c8b29a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b17175d0a375b3ed5e81597dac4983fdb46e478d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/791941be5da125d9a1b228582bfdc300c05d05b3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e6c2e6c2e1fa066968a16aca1cb66cd1bdde7741"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-53374", "GHSA-45w5-677j-gmrq"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "28d11336-65cd-39ee-b49f-109ce8b8fb0c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d38ceaf99ed015f2a0b9af3499791bd3a3daae21 <8ae8b9e74bab94aab1d79f1688129bcc61c8b29a"}, {"id": "28d1b565-5638-3037-8e42-83930ea7c2b6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d38ceaf99ed015f2a0b9af3499791bd3a3daae21 <e6c2e6c2e1fa066968a16aca1cb66cd1bdde7741"}, {"id": "5d240c74-ff2b-3774-b9d9-f51d667d8b78", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.175"}, {"id": "70f0be50-0932-39b5-bda9-f9233a5e408c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.9"}, {"id": "8bd8a734-0a63-318d-9f96-1a8da7941edd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "958077b6-c77d-3548-ab31-ee76170e6ade", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "a38f1826-3b41-3e78-90b5-2de16582da9e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.90"}, {"id": "b17fe216-c815-358f-95f5-f738cb3e13cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.140"}, {"id": "c700a3f7-5d9f-31ee-9b52-e7d6071864e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.2"}, {"id": "d3277837-239c-3d37-a0c3-c0882ac5736d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d38ceaf99ed015f2a0b9af3499791bd3a3daae21 <b17175d0a375b3ed5e81597dac4983fdb46e478d"}, {"id": "da332f7c-afec-30fc-9cd1-639fc1f9ab55", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d38ceaf99ed015f2a0b9af3499791bd3a3daae21 <91fbb5e635c8fb1b49e15c19da06480089ef719f"}, {"id": "eb5d2408-60e9-37ea-bb20-78cf2e1a8bad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d38ceaf99ed015f2a0b9af3499791bd3a3daae21 <40df11255d71b02e20e70579f1b12b687e396e26"}, {"id": "efb897a8-be94-3a4c-a1dc-8a201a64b235", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.32"}, {"id": "f23b5846-095f-378c-81e6-1c44869a0a50", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Li